      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. The maximum single dose is typically 850\u20131,000 mg. This order is about twice the daily maximum, and a 1,700 mg dose is well above the single-dose limit. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI effects.\n\nCould this be a transcription error? Some possibilities:\n- 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day), the maximum dose\n- 850 mg twice daily (1,700 mg/day total)\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg three times daily or twice daily\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into divided doses\n\nPlease tell me the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order."
      }
